{"id":"word:hebrew:H5514","type":"word","title":"סִינַי","subtitle":"H5514 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Sinai , mountain of Arabia","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to סִינַי (H5514) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-loc.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 35 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"סִינַי (Çîynay) means Sinai , mountain of Arabia First listed occurrence: Deut 33 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"סִינַי","transliteration":"Çîynay","pronunciation":"see-nah'-ee","strong":"H5514","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5514","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-loc","forms":["סִינָֽי","סִינַ֔י","סִינָ֑י","סִינַ֖י","סִינַי֙"],"morphs":[["HNp",34],["HR/Np",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"Sinai , mountain of Arabia","usage":"Sinai.","full":"H5514. Sinay סִינַי proper name, of a mountain Sinai ; — name of mountain of law-giving in J and especially P ( חֹרֵב in E and especially D): Judg 5:5 ; Psa 68:9 ; Deut 33:2 (poem), also Exod 16:1 (P); usually הַרסִֿינַי ( סִֿינָ֑י Lev 7:38 +), rarely J, Exod 19:20 , 23 and perhaps 34:2 , 4 , elsewhere mostly P, 24:16 ; 31:18 ; 34:29 , 32 ; Lev 7:38 ; 25:1 ; 27:34 ; and 26:46 (H), Num 3:1 ; 28:6 , also Neh 9:13 ; סִינַי מִרְבַּר ( סִינָ֑י Num 1:19 +), Exod 19:1-2 , Lev 7:38 ; Num 1:1 , 19 ; 3:4 , 14 ; 9:1 , 5 ; 10:12 ; 26:64 ; 33:15-16 , (all P); — in view of these facts, and of E's use of חֹרֵב (q. v.), it is probably that Exod 19:11 , 18 (in E passages) are from R. — ᵐ5 Σ ( ε ) ινα . Identification dubious; local tradition names Jebel Musa , mountain at southern end of peninsular between the two arms of Red Sea, so Rob BR i. 90 ff., especially 119-122 compare Stanley Sinai and Pal. 42 f. and elsewhere , specifically its northern spur, Ras ‚afƒâfeh ; but Lepsius Briefe 345 ff., 416 ff. Eb GS especially 392 ff. and others advocate Serbal , northwest from Jebel Musa (on tradition, cf Eb ib. 413 ff. ); see discussion Di 19:1 . Against both is the working of Egyptian mines in the peninsula as late as the 19th dynasty (see Eb GS 135, 148 ff., 159, etc. ), involving presence of soldiers there. This, and connection with Midian (compare also Judg 5:5 ), have led to search for Sinai further northeast, near head of Gulf of Akaba, or even in Seir, so Say Monuments 263 ff. , compare GFM 5:5 ; 6:1 and Yakut , cited by Id 179n. § , also see Gall Altisr. Kultst. 12 ; on sanctity of the mountain see further RS Sem i. 110 f., 2nd ed. 177 f. Sm Rel. Geschichte. 30 .","rootNote":"of uncertain derivation;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"Deut 33 2","keyReferences":["Deut 33 2","Exod 16 1","Exod 19 1","Exod 19 2","Exod 19 11","Exod 19 18","Exod 19 20","Exod 19 23"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":35,"occurrences":[{"reference":"Deut 33 2","book":"Deut","chapter":33,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מִ/סִּינַ֥י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Np"},{"reference":"Exod 16 1","book":"Exod","chapter":16,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"סִינָ֑י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"Exod 19 1","book":"Exod","chapter":19,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"סִינָֽי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"Exod 19 2","book":"Exod","chapter":19,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"סִינַ֔י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"Exod 19 11","book":"Exod","chapter":19,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"סִינָֽי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"Exod 19 18","book":"Exod","chapter":19,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"סִינַי֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"Exod 19 20","book":"Exod","chapter":19,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"סִינַ֖י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"Exod 19 23","book":"Exod","chapter":19,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"סִינָ֑י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":